ment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Action Verbs Used in Programming in Present, Past and Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Here are some of the many verbs you can use when describing programming languages. You can use these verbs to describe how OOP works. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The brochure says that many apps, such as Textfield and Array, are using this OOP. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "People who program with OOP decided long ago to divide  information in objects, which they defined as encapsulated data."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this chart, you will find the basic forms of verbs in English language that will help you describe OOP. It is very important to highlight that verbs will change depending on the grammar structure that the specific tense requires. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Base Form </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Tense* </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Past Tense** </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Past Participle** </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> -ing Form </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To design</br> To define</br> To characterize</br> To fill</br> To create</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Design/ designs</br>  Define/ defines</br>  Characterize/ characterizes</br>  Fill/fills</br>  Create/ creates</br> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Designed</br> Defined</br> Characterized</br> Filled</br> Created</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Designed</br> Defined</br> Characterized</br> Filled</br> Created</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Designing</br> Defining Characterizing</br> Filling</br> Creating</br>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "*Remember that for constructing a sentence in simple present tense, it is vital to be careful when conjugating the verb in third person singular since there is a variation for this particular case (you add and -s or an \u2013es at the end). </br></br> **When using the past tense in English, we have to take into account that there are <span class=\"italic\"> irregular </span> and <span class=\"italic\"> regular </span> verbs and their structure is different. In this case, the chart only shows how regular verbs work (the suffix \u2013ed is added). "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modal Verb Must"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " The modal verb <span class=\"strong\">must</span> has different uses. The most common use refers to expressing that something is mandatory, like an obligation or duty. You can use this grammatical construction  when talking about the elements or essential features that a programming paradigm as OOP has. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In programming terminology, an object is a component that must contain properties and methods needed to make data useful."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When talking about the washing machine, properties must be all the features related to height, weight, price and brand."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take a look at the following grammatical structure: </br> </br>  <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">  must </span>+ verb in present tense + complement </div> </br></br> <div class=\"center_text\"> Example:<br/> </br>  <div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\"> You <span class=\"strong\"> must </span> know how classes and objects work in OOP. </span> </div> </br></br>  The following chart shows other uses for the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">must</span>: </br> </br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Use </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Example </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Obligation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The students <span class=\\\"strong\\\">  must </span> take the exam before graduating. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Strong recommendation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> must </span> stop smoking; it's for your own health. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Deduction\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Lauren is pale, she <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> must </span> be sick. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "come across "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to  find something or someone by chance"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I came across this brochure about OOP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "displayed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "placed somewhere to be easily seen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was a bunch of these displayed in the main hall of the faculty. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le02ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "portray "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to represent or describe someone or something through a painting, film